Zero BIOS VBE graphics - independent component checks
Date: 2026-11-15

Implementation
bios.zero now queries VBE2/3, follows the actual far mode list, validates a
32-bit RGB/BGR linear mode, prefers800x600 and falls back to640..800 by480..600.
Unsupported firmware preserves a VGA text handoff. BIOS64 maps the first4GiB
using page directories3000/4000/5000/c000; no real-mode table store exceeds
64KiB. The shared128-byte handoff also provides stack pool40000..8ffff.
BIOS-GRAPHICS.txt specifies the constraints and memory layout.

Final component binary
The latest compiler candidate build/selfhost-core-threads-stage2 includes the
physical-address guard in far16. It compiled current bios.zero to10947 bytes,
within the16384-byte El Torito slot. Exact source/compiler/binary/probe-ISO
hashes are in final-input-sha256.txt. The private probe ISO is not the release
ISO: it contains the standalone pixel probe as both raw kernel payloads.
No assembler or linker was invoked. The probe and loader are Zero source;
the existing own Zero ISO writer built the optical container.

PASS final BIOS32
SeaBIOS/stdVGA, CPU qemu64,-lm,-pae: entered protected32 mode, obtained800x600
BGR framebuffer, and wrote every pixel using the supplied stride. Only after
all writes finished did the Zero probe report BIOS GRAPHICS PROBE PASS.
Evidence: final32.serial, final32.png.

PASS final BIOS64
SeaBIOS/stdVGA, CPU qemu64: entered long mode and completed the same800x600
pixel writes. final64-handoff.txt records framebuffer0xfd000000, beyond the
old1GiB identity mapping, stride800, format1BGR and architecture64. It also
records the stack pool base40000 and size50000. The final32/final64 raw PPM
screen captures are byte-identical; their PNGs were viewed and show the
expected independently colored horizontal/vertical gradient.
Evidence: final64.serial, final64.png, final64-handoff.txt.

Additional development checks
The first VBE implementation selected640x480; the same full-pixel probe passed
in both BIOS32 and BIOS64, with identical screens. Those results are retained
as bios32/bios64.*. The subsequent800x600 preference passed both modes as
preferred32/preferred64.* before the final far16-guard candidate was retested
above. Both tested resolutions use the same kernel-side pixel ABI.

ISA VGA fallback
A separate private ISO combined the initial new BIOS component with the
unchanged0.5 kernel. SeaBIOS with ISA VGA and the ISA VGA option ROM had no
eligible32-bit linear mode; the loader retained kind1,baseb8000,stride80.
The existing visible VGA terminal booted, mounted ZeroFS and reached zero>.
Evidence: text-fallback.serial, text-fallback.png, text-fallback-handoff.txt.
The only writable data disk was a private copy of build/data.img.

VirtualBox-firmware limitation observed
Official VirtualBox7.2 PC BIOS and VGA ROMs were also run on QEMU stdVGA
hardware. In that combination VBE4F00 left the request buffer unchanged,
so no VESA controller response existed and the loader correctly retained
text mode. The framebuffer-only probe therefore reported FAIL, as expected
for a non-framebuffer handoff. This is NOT a VirtualBox graphics success and
is not native VirtualBox testing. Evidence: vbox32-video-query.txt and
vbox32.serial. The ROM/device mismatch must not be represented as proof of
native VirtualBox VBE behavior. The standard SeaBIOS/stdVGA paths passed.

Environment and reproduction
QEMU10.0.13, pc machine, TCG,128MiB, one CPU, no network. External test tools:
/workspace/qemu-local/root/usr/bin/qemu-system-x86_64
/workspace/qemu-local/root/usr/share/qemu
/workspace/qemu-local/root/usr/share/seabios/bios-256k.bin
/workspace/qemu-local/root/usr/share/seabios/vgabios-stdvga.bin
LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/workspace/qemu-local/root/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu

Compile bios.zero with --real and pixel-probe.zero with --raw/--raw32. Pad
BIOS to16384 bytes and each raw probe to131072 bytes. Pipe these three slots
and the existing16777216-byte system.img to build/iso. Attach the resulting
private image read-only as IDE secondary-master CD-ROM, no data disk:
-machine pc -accel tcg -m128 -display none -nic none -no-reboot -boot order=d
-bios BIOS_ROM -vga none -device VGA,romfile=VGA_ROM -cpu CPU
-serial file:TRANSCRIPT -monitor tcp:127.0.0.1:PORT,server=on,wait=off
-drive file=PROBE_ISO,format=raw,media=cdrom,if=ide,index=2,readonly=on
After PASS, the monitor screendump command captured the image and quit ended
each process. All test VMs are stopped. Original data.img/data.vdi were not
modified. The final integrated operating-system release has separate tests.
